    {
      "version": "0.6.0",
      "date": "2026-11-02T17:22:08.846Z",
      "notes": "- Google Drive backups per profile: snapshots go to the profile's own Drive folder (no Drive desktop app needed), with restore, download and the newer-backup check at startup. CLI: nexus snapshot drive.\n- New profiles can start from a copy of an existing Nexus database file (checked, then copied); each profile needs its own backup folder.\n- Task List: folded groups are remembered, each group has its own \"+ New Task\" pre-filled with the group's value, and a new task starts with the values of single-value filters.\n- Completed tasks are hidden in the list and the kanban unless \"Show completed\" is on or a filter asks for them.\n- Pick lists of more than three values filter as you type.\n- Desktop: a Projects popup chooses which projects lie on the desk (filter, All / None / Only these). CLI: nexus desk projects.\n- Monthly routines can start on a day of the month (\"every month from the 15th\").\n- Profiles: pick the icon from the icon popup. File dialogs open on the app window.",
